#---HelloWorldPlugin.test----------------------- Executable,LS -----------------#
#BEGIN_COMMENT
# Example plugin-local test. This is intended to be a template for upstream
# plugins: compile a small input, load the plugin through its YAML configuration,
# and verify registration, initialization, execution, and cleanup through the
# standard ELD lit substitutions.
#END_COMMENT
#START_TEST
RUN: %clang %clangopts -c "%p/Inputs/hello.c" -o "%t.o"
RUN: %link %linkopts "%t.o" -e main -o "%t.out" --plugin-config "%p/../HelloWorldPlugin.yaml" --trace=plugin 2>&1 | %filecheck "%s"
#END_TEST

CHECK: Note: Found plugin handler for plugin type HelloWorldPlugin in Library
CHECK: Trace: Calling HelloWorldPlugin::Init plugin hook
CHECK: Trace: Calling plugin hook handler HelloWorldPlugin::VisitSections
CHECK: Trace: Calling plugin hook handler HelloWorldPlugin::ActBeforeRuleMatching
CHECK: Trace: Calling plugin hook handler HelloWorldPlugin::ActBeforeSectionMerging
CHECK: Trace: Calling plugin hook handler HelloWorldPlugin::ActBeforePerformingLayout
CHECK: Trace: Calling plugin hook handler HelloWorldPlugin::ActBeforeWritingOutput
CHECK: Trace: Calling HelloWorldPlugin::Destroy plugin hook
